{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the Mishkan you shall make, ten panels.</b> These are the lower ones, called Mishkan because the tablets and the ark and the holy vessels, in which the Shekhinah dwells, are placed beneath them." "<b>Twisted linen.</b> Rashi explained: each kind of thread is doubled sixfold. In tractate Yoma, chapter Ba Lo, it is derived from verses." "<b>Work of a weaver.</b> This is weaving work that requires planning, but work of an embroiderer is needlework and does not require planning."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:32.443350526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}